The remainder when \(f(x)\) is divided by \(x^2 - 1\) is of the form \(ax + b\). Evaluating \(f(x)\) at the roots \(x = 1\) and \(x = -1\) gives:

\[
\begin{aligned}
f(1) &= 1 + 5 - 8 + 7 - 1 - 12 + 4 - 8 + 12 - 5 - 5 = -10, \\
f(-1) &= 1 - 5 - 8 - 7 - 1 + 12 + 4 + 8 + 12 + 5 - 5 = 16.
\end{aligned}
\]

This yields the system:
\[
\begin{cases}
a + b = -10 \\
-a + b = 16
\end{cases}
\]
Solving gives \(b = 3\) and \(a = -13\). Therefore, the remainder is \(-13x + 3\).

\boxed{-13x+3}

